#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ha: the one safe CLI for the owner's Home Assistant (HA OS VM; URL: profile services.ha_url).

Reads (output always passes the privacy gate, ~/bin/lib/ha_privacy.py):
  ha state <entity_id|name> [--json]       one entity in detail (several name matches: a short list)
  ha list [domain] [--area AREA] [--json]  one line per entity: id, state, name, area
  ha find "<words>" [--domain D] [--json]  fuzzy match on friendly name, entity id and area
  ha areas                                 areas with entity counts per domain
  ha device-url <entity> [--json]          its device's configuration_url (LAN http only, e.g. a WLED's own
                                           web/JSON API): printed as scheme://host[:port], the one output that
                                           is not IP-masked; anything that is not a LAN URL is refused
History (read-only; same gate: location, network, notification and Bluetooth entities stay hidden):
  ha history <entity> [--since 24h|90m|7d|HH:MM|ISO] [--until ...] [--attrs a,b] [--limit N] [--json]
                                           state changes (recorder, /api/history/period, minimal_response;
                                           --attrs: also those gated attributes, every update) with durations
  ha logbook [entity] [--since ...] [--until ...] [--limit N] [--json]
                                           logbook entries (who/what changed it); hidden entities are left out
  ha trace <automation|script> [--last N] [--json]
                                           the last N stored runs (websocket trace/list + trace/get), summarised:
                                           trigger, conditions passed/failed, actions run, errors (never variables
                                           or service data)
Writes (allowlisted domains/services, one unambiguous target, logged, read back old -> new):
  ha on|off|toggle <target>...             or: ha on|off|toggle --area AREA [--domain light]
  ha set <light>|--area AREA [--brightness 0-100] [--color-temp KELVIN] [--color NAME]
  ha media <player> play|pause|stop|next|prev|mute|unmute|volume N     (N = 0-100)
  ha scene run <scene>        ha script run <script>
  ha call <domain.service> <entity> ['{"json": "data"}']
To-do lists (only the lists in TODO_LISTS, default todo.shopping_list; more via ~/.config/ha/todo-lists.json
{"lists": ["todo.x"]} or HA_TODO_LISTS=a,b): items are the owner's own list entries, printed through the gate
  ha todo items [--list L] [--all] [--json]   open items (--all: completed too): uid, status, summary, description
  ha todo add "<item>" [--description T] [--list L] [--json]   adds one item; prints its uid (exit 3: not seen)
  ha todo done|undo|rm <uid|summary> [--list L] [--json]      tick off / reopen / remove one item (read back)
  write options: -n/--dry-run (resolve + show, send nothing), --wait S (read-back timeout, default 8),
                 --owner-ok "his words" (only for garage/gate/door-named covers, switches, buttons)
Exit: 0 ok, 1 HA/connection error, 2 refused/ambiguous/usage, 3 sent but new state not confirmed.

Safety by construction: every request passes check_request() before a byte is sent. REST for everything
except traces:
GET /api/states[/<entity>], GET /api/config/script/config/<id> (lock/garage check before a script runs),
POST /api/template with the fixed AREA_TEMPLATE or DEVICE_URL_TEMPLATE (one validated entity id), POST /api/services/<domain>/<service> for the
SERVICES allowlist (light switch input_boolean media_player remote scene script cover climate fan vacuum
button update.install, todo add/update/remove/get_items; input_text, select and input_datetime only on the few
helper/mode entities listed in INPUT_TEXT_WRITABLE, SELECT_WRITABLE, INPUT_DATETIME_WRITABLE) with an entity_id of that same domain and no target-redirecting keys;
`?return_response` only for todo.get_items; todo calls target exactly one TODO_LISTS list with item fields only. No other websocket command, no config or
registry writes (that is ha-apply's job), no raw state dumps. Read-only extras: GET /api/history/period/<ts> for
exactly one entity (filter_entity_id, end_time, minimal_response, no_attributes, significant_changes_only=0) and
GET /api/logbook/<ts> (end_time, entity); websocket only for trace/list and trace/get (automation|script, one item,
check_ws()); its auth message is the handshake, not a command. lock and alarm_control_panel are never
controllable; garage/gate/door covers, switches, buttons and update.install need --owner-ok; scenes/scripts that touch
locks/alarms (or garages, without --owner-ok) are refused.
Log: ~/.local/state/ha/actions.log (JSON lines: time, service, entity_ids, data, result, old -> new).
Token: ~/.secrets/ha-admin-token (never printed). Tests: ~/opt/ha-tests/run.sh (fake HA).
Env (tests): HA_URL, HA_TOKEN_FILE, HA_STATE_DIR, HA_TODO_LISTS, HA_TODO_CONFIG.
"""
import argparse
import base64
import contextlib
